**Note on the problem statement:** $SU(3) \times SU(3)$ is **not** a simple Lie group (it is semisimple), and $\pi_3(SU(3) \times SU(3)) = \mathbb{Z} \oplus \mathbb{Z}$, not $\mathbb{Z}$. I will solve the problem using the correct mathematics and note where the stated $\pi_3(G)=\mathbb{Z}$ would lead to the same conclusion.

